{title: Did You Think to Pray}
{artist: Mary A. Kidder / William O. Perkins}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Church Gospel Songs and Hymns, Verna E. Howard & Broadus E. Smith (West Monroe, Louisiana: Central Printers & Publishers, 1983), # 39)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Ere you left your room this morning,
[C7]Did you think [F]to [C]pray?
[C]In the name of [Am]Christ our [F]Savior,
[F]Did you sue for loving [Bb]favor,
[C7]As a shield to[F]day?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]O how praying rests the weary!
[F]Prayer will change the night to [C]day;
[F]So when life seems dark and [Bb]dreary,
[C7]Don’t forget to [F]pray.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]When you met with great temptation,
[C7]Did you think [F]to [C]pray?
[C]By His dying [Am]love and [F]merit,
[F]Did you claim the Holy [Bb]Spirit
[C7]As your guide and [F]stay?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]When your heart was filled with anger,
[C7]Did you think [F]to [C]pray?
[C]Did you plead for [Am]grace, my [F]brother,
[F]That you might forgive a[Bb]nother
[C7]Who had crossed your [F]way?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]When sore trials came upon you,
[C7]Did you think [F]to [C]pray?
[C]When your soul was [Am]bowed in [F]sorrow,
[F]Balm of Gilead did you [Bb]borrow
[C7]At the gates of [F]day?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
